 "caption": "Dissolved CO₂ exists as CO₂(aq), HCO₃⁻ and CO₃²⁻ in proportions set by pH. They cross at pKa₁ = 6.35 and pKa₂ = 10.33. At seawater's pH of about 8.1, hydrogencarbonate dominates; as the ocean acidifies, carbonate falls, which harms shell-building organisms.",
